On Mon, Nov 16, 2026 at 7:02 PM Tomas wrote:
> What about `a?.b` for attribute access that returns None when `a` is None?

I like the idea, but I think the spelling matters less than the rules for
chains. If `a?.b.c` short-circuits the whole chain, then it is easy to explain;
if only `b` is guarded, people will be surprised when `.c` raises.

A small table of examples in the PEP draft would help a lot.

Priya

